urkish Kol böreği and the Greek spanakopita."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bulemas"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulemas"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Sephardic Jewish cuisine","cuisine/sephardic-jewish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Feta cheese","ingredient/feta-cheese"],["Kashkaval","ingredient/kashkaval"]]},{"h":"More from Sephardic Jewish cuisine","links":[["Apio (appetizer)","dish/apio-appetizer"],["Fritas de prasa","dish/fritas-de-prasa"]]}]},"dish/candlenut-kitchen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/candlenut-kitchen","n":"Candlenut Kitchen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Peranakan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Candlenut Kitchen, often known simply as Candlenut, is a Singaporean restaurant serving the local Peranakan cuisine. Located at the Tanglin district, the restaurant is owned by Malcolm Lee, who also serves as its executive chef."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-candlenut-kitchen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlenut_Kitchen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Peranakan cuisine","cuisine/peranakan-cuisine"]]}]},"dish/carbonara":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/carbonara","n":"Carbonara","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Carbonara is a pasta dish made with cured pork, hard cheese, eggs, salt, and black pepper. It is typical of the Lazio region of Italy. The dish took its modern form and name in the middle of the 20th century."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-carbonara"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbonara"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Guanciale","ingredient/guanciale"],["Pancetta","ingredient/pancetta"],["Pasta","ingredient/pasta"],["Pecorino","ingredient/pecorino"],["Pecorino romano","ingredient/pecorino-romano"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Spaghetti","ingredient/spaghetti"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["5-8 Club","dish/5-8-club"],["Altabira City Tavern","dish/altabira-city-tavern"],["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Applebee's","dish/applebee-s"],["Arby's","dish/arby-s"],["Arnold's Bar and Grill","dish/arnold-s-bar-and-grill"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Ben's Chili Bowl","dish/ben-s-chili-bowl"],["Benjy's","dish/benjy-s"],["Besaw's","dish/besaw-s"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blackhawk (restaurant)","dish/blackhawk-restaurant"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Bobcat Bite","dish/bobcat-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/brown-derby"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Busboys and Poets","dish/busboys-and-poets"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Byways Cafe","dish/byways-cafe"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["California Grill","dish/california-grill"],["Camp Washington Chili","dish/camp-washington-chili"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carnation Cafe","dish/carnation-cafe"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chiltern Firehouse","dish/chiltern-firehouse"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/33/Espaguetis_carbonara.jpg/500px-Espaguetis_carbonara.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Javier Somoza","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Espaguetis_carbonara.jpg"}},"ingredient/sodium-chloride":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sodium-chloride","n":"Sodium chloride","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Sodium chloride, is an ionic compound with the chemical formula NaCl, representing a 1:1 ratio of sodium and chloride ions. It is transparent or translucent, brittle, hygroscopic, and occurs as the mineral halite. In its edible form, common table salt, it is commonly used as a condiment and food preservative. Large quantities of sodium chloride are used in many industrial processes, and it is a major source of sodium and chlorine compounds used as feedstocks for further chemical syntheses. Another major application of sodium chloride is de-icing of roadways in sub-freezing weather."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sodium-chloride"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_chloride"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Bengali cuisine","cuisine/bengali-cuisine",[["Chutney","dish/chutney"]]],["Kerala cuisine","cuisine/kerala-cuisine",[["Chutney","dish/chutney"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/7c/Selpologne.jpg/500px-Selpologne.jpg","w":500,"h":474,"by":"Didier Descouens","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Selpologne.jpg"}},"dish/curry-in-the-united-kingdom":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/curry-in-the-united-kingdom","n":"Curry in the United Kingdom","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from British cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Curry, a spicy dish derived from Indian cuisine by way of British Raj–era Anglo-Indian cuisine, is popular in the United Kingdom. Curry recipes have been printed in Britain since 1747, when Hannah Glasse gave a recipe for a chicken \"currey the India way\". Curry powder was first advertised in 1784. In the 19th century, many more recipes appeared in the popular cookery books of the time. Curries in Britain are widely described with Indian terms, not necessarily used for the same dishes or even known in India. For example, korma is a mild sauce with almond and coconut; Madras has a hot, slightly sour sauce; phall denotes an extra hot sauce, and pasanda means a mild sauce with cream and coconut milk. One type of curry, chicken tikka masala, has become widespread enough to be described as a national dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-curry-in-the-united-kingdom"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curry_in_the_United_Kingdom"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great British Chef